# Cloudflare Workers static-asset redirects.
# Everything here is a 301 because these URLs are dead for good, and a 301 is what
# passes ranking to the replacement. If a rule ever needs to be temporary, use 302.
#
# Every target carries a trailing slash. Workers static assets serve
# public/<slug>/index.html at "/<slug>/" and 307 "/<slug>" to it, so a target
# written without the slash turns one redirect into a 301 -> 307 chain.

# --- host: www folds into the apex ---------------------------------------------
# Removed 31 Jul 2026. Workers static assets only accept relative sources here, so
# wrangler rejects the whole file if this line is present. It was never live either
# way — www.itsnum.com returned 200 rather than a 301. The www fold belongs in a
# zone-level Redirect Rule (Rules > Redirect Rules), not in _redirects. Until that
# rule exists, www serves the site directly; canonical tags point at the apex.

